---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../config/site';

const updated = '7 November 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description={`How ${SITE_NAME} handles your data.`}>
  <div class="container prose">
    <p class="draft" role="note">
      <strong>Draft for review.</strong> This policy is an honest first draft written before ads or
      leaderboards are switched on. Please review and have it checked before launch.
    </p>

    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="prose__meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      Right now {SITE_NAME} does not have accounts, does not run ads, and does not send your activity
      to any server. A few small things are saved on your own device so the games remember your
      progress. That's it.
    </p>

    <h2>What we store on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Using your browser's local storage (not cookies), {SITE_NAME} keeps, only on your device:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>your best scores for each game;</li>
      <li>your sound on/off preference;</li>
      <li>your daily puzzle streak and which daily puzzles you've finished;</li>
      <li>whether you've seen a game's how-to-play screen.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This data never leaves your device and is not shared. Clearing your browser's site data removes
      it, which also resets your scores and streak.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      There is no analytics or tracking today. If a privacy-friendly analytics tool is added later, it
      will be described here first, and it will not identify you personally.
    </p>

    <h2>Ads (planned, not yet active)</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} plans to show ads in future to help cover costs. No ad code loads today. When ads
      are turned on, they are expected to be served by Google AdSense (and possibly Google's H5 Games
      Ads for between-game breaks). Those services may set cookies or use device identifiers to show
      and measure ads.
    </p>
    <p>
      For visitors in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland, a Google-certified consent banner will ask for
      your choices before any ad code loads. This section will be rewritten with the exact details
      when ads go live.
    </p>

    <h2>Leaderboards (planned, not yet active)</h2>
    <p>
      Global high-score tables are planned. When they launch, submitting a score would store a display
      name you choose and the score itself on our backend. Playing without submitting will remain
      possible. This section will be updated with specifics at that time.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is a general-audience arcade. It does not knowingly collect personal information
      from anyone, including children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      As features like ads and leaderboards are added, this policy will be updated and the date above
      changed. Significant changes will be noted on the site.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    padding-top: var(--sp-6);
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: var(--sp-6);
  }
  .prose__meta {
    color: var(--ticket-dim);
    font-size: var(--fs-0);
  }
  .prose ul {
    color: var(--ticket-dim);
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-1);
  }
  .draft {
    padding: var(--sp-3) var(--sp-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--marquee);
    border-radius: var(--r-button);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--marquee) 10%, transparent);
    color: var(--ticket);
  }
</style>
